# Build Risk Guard

Pre-flight checks to avoid the recurring build hazards in this repo. Apply before running builds/tests and before declaring work done.

## Shell: PowerShell has no `&&`

The default shell is PowerShell. Chaining with `&&` fails ("not a valid statement separator").

```powershell
# ❌ BAD
cargo fmt --check && cargo clippy -- -D warnings

# ✅ GOOD — sequence with ; and gate on $LASTEXITCODE
cargo fmt --check; if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit $LASTEXITCODE }
cargo clippy -- -D warnings; if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit $LASTEXITCODE }
```

## Locked desktop binary (`os error 5: Access is denied`)

A running `ade-desktop-app.exe` locks its target file and breaks `cargo build/test --workspace`.

- Before a workspace build/test, confirm the desktop app is not running (check for the process), or
- Scope commands to avoid it: `cargo build --workspace --exclude ade-desktop-app`.
- `os error 5` on `ade-desktop-app.exe` is an environment lock, not a compile error — do not "fix" code for it.

## Money: never reintroduce `f64`

All monetary values use `ade_core::Money` (i64 micro-dollars). Convert `f64`/USD strings only at the UI/CLI boundary; never do financial arithmetic in `f64`.

## const fn: no non-const trait methods

Avoid `Ord::max`/`min` etc. in `const fn` (not const-stable). Use explicit branches: `if x < 0 { 0 } else { x }`.

## Definition of done (verify ladder)

Before claiming completion, run and pass:
`cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test`, and `tsc --noEmit` in `apps/desktop`. Never disable a lint/security tool to make a build pass.

## Safety invariants

Never commit two write-capable agents on one checkout. Never read/quote secrets (`.env`, `*.pem`, `*.key`, `*credentials*.json`). Never merge/deploy without human approval.
